<title>UK: Shell says all Nigeria flow stations now operating.</title>
<headline>Shell says all Nigeria flow stations now operating.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell said on Wednesday all its Nigerian flow stations were back in operation.</p>
<p>&quot;Egwa and Odidi are now back up,&quot; said a Shell spokesman.</p>
<p>The two were the last of a string of flow stations to resume operations after being occupied last week by villagers in a local political protest which cut Shell's Nigerian output by as much as 210,000 bpd.</p>
<p>Shell said on Tuesday that all its operations were returning gradually to normal and that production would resume full flow this week.</p>
<p>Four early April Bonny light cargoes were delayed by three days as a result of the disruption.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8060</p>
